`parse_fragment` yields blocks in source order. It first yields `Magic.parse(parser)`, so block 0 dispatches to `Magic.write_into`, which is defined on `Magic`. Then, after the header, the body loop for this input yields a cue, then a comment block for `NOTE`, then another cue. `CueBlock` defines its own `write_into`, so both cue blocks dispatch to `CueBlock.write_into`. `CommentBlock` does not override `write_into`, so its call resolves by inheritance to `Block.write_into`.

